cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Praukron in your work, please cite it.
title: "Praukron: repository-native project memory and governance for human-AI software development"
abstract: >-
  Praukron is a repository-native project-state protocol and reference
  implementation for asynchronous human-AI software development. It keeps
  people and coding agents working from the same explicit project state by
  storing phases, tasks, dependencies, decisions, acceptance contracts and
  evidence as versioned Markdown inside the repository. A deterministic
  compiler derives project state from those records and projects it as an
  interactive dashboard for humans and structured context for agents. Praukron
  is designed to preserve project authority, causal history and definition of
  done across asynchronous human and AI work without relying on hidden agent
  memory.
type: software
authors:
